# thinking — a principled means refuses a crime while it is thought out, not after the click
#
# Ripelore chooses to steal from the chest and Discipline, a high-morality action modus mentis, is
# pinned as the means. HighMoralityRefusesCrimeRule refuses it during the think, unasked: the
# refusal is narrated and no button is produced — the act is never offered, so no point can be
# spent attempting it. The refusal reaches the proposal ledger like any other: Scientific Research,
# a different mind, is still offered stealing, and since it was refused once already this phase the
# means is narrowed to those the willingness rules let through. `means none` hands the draw back to
# the RNG, so the button can only appear if that narrowing kept Discipline out.
#
# Buttons are asserted as "] <goal>" — the tail of "[Snatch ●] steal …" — which the prose never
# contains.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Room" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Chest" --grant-mm discipline,snatch,scientific_research --means-only discipline

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal steal
advance 12 180

# Ripelore; Discipline refuses to steal, before any button exists.
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect against every principle I hold
expect-not ] steal

# Scientific Research: still offered stealing, carried out by a means that would not refuse.
means none
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 2
advance 12 180
expect ] steal

quit
